- op: discuss  # d76a
  at: '2026-07-12T05:36:58Z'  # d76a
  by: agent  # d76a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d76a
  clock: 4  # d76a
  nonce: d76a  # d76a
  message: "Owner decision 2026-07-12 (design walkthrough): DEFER the entire ADR-0042 survey-rename campaign (S2-S8: constant+import shim, WI-vatuf CLI default+verb, docs sweep, test/scripts sweep, tracker sweep) to the END of Wave 5. Rationale: (1) the campaign full forward isbefore-closure blocks ZERO P1 items -- verified, the closure is 5 self-contained P2/P3 nodes with nothing outside the campaign -- so deferring has no critical-path cost. (2) Ratified-but-unstarted P3 mechanical churn (~65 script refs + docs + fixtures + ~52 tracker items); payoff is naming coherence, not correctness. (3) Executing it LAST is strictly better than now: ADR-0042 sec.4 merges the two divergent resolvers (_discover_input_file + find_behavior_map) and touches cli.py heavily, which would collide with the P1 cli.py/resolver structural work; doing it after that settles avoids the overlap. The 7 todo_soft leaves set to someday + tagged wave5. ADR-0042 stays Accepted and banked; INV-firuh stays violated until S1-S8 land at end of Wave 5."  # d76a
- op: discuss  # 4ded
  at: '2026-07-14T17:57:32Z'  # 4ded
  by: agent  # 4ded
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4ded
  clock: 5  # 4ded
  nonce: 4ded  # 4ded
  message: "S2/S3 FOUNDATION LANDED (2026-07-14, PR merged to dev @ f094e027c7). The canonical-name constant + merged discovery resolver shipped: behavior_map_io.CANONICAL_SURVEY_FILENAME='survey.json' + LEGACY_SURVEY_FILENAMES (hypergumbo.results.json / hg.json / bm.json / behavior_map.json) + SURVEY_FILENAMES + find_survey_in_dir() (canonical-first, plain-over-gz, name-major); cli._discover_input_file rewired onto it (widens auto-discovery to the canonical name + all legacy aliases; no user-facing change). find_behavior_map's single-basename signature + its bakeoff-script callers deliberately left untouched (the bakeoff-side resolver merge is a separate PR to isolate the editable-install shim-first hazard). 11 TDD tests, 100% coverage.\n\nCOLLISION-RISK VERIFICATION (2026-07-14): the 2026-07-12 deferral cited collision with 'the P1 cli.py/resolver structural work'. ADR-0042 §4 names that work: the resolver-merge is the joint deliverable with cli-input:F3 under the INV-fabov umbrella. INV-fabov is SATISFIED (2026-07-10, PR #538); load_substrate + SubstrateError shipped; no open P1 cli.py/resolver-structural item. So the collision premise is resolved and the campaign is unblocked. Resumed at owner request with the foundational internal PR first, reassessing before the outward-facing WI-vatuf change.\n\nREMAINING (INV-firuh stays violated until S1-S8 all land): WI-vatuf (CLI default filename + survey verb, OUTWARD-FACING), WI-didif (legacy-filename acceptance + deprecation warnings), WI-kisoj (run_behavior_map->run_survey + behavior_map_io.py->survey_io.py rename), WI-gakih (test fixtures / bm.json), WI-rivuj (docs sweep; .agent/ portion = separate human-approved PR), WI-zaviv (spec stability-commitment language), WI-goril (tracker sweep). The ~100+ hardcoded refs the sweeps target: bakeoff-deep 27, bakeoff-broad 18, cli.py 16, analyze-artifacts 7, sketch.py 4, hypergumbo_diag.py 5, + docs/tests/~52 tracker items."  # 4ded
